  Arguments: int index
  Returns: -
  Description: Let FL Studio dispatch OnDirtyMixerTrack event to all midi devices. Use index = -1 for all tracks
  API version: 1

isAssigned() -> int
  Arguments: -
  Returns: int
  Description: Returns True if (linked) output interface is assigned.
  API version: 1

isDoubleClick(int index) -> int
  Arguments: int index
  Returns: int
  Description: Returns True if the function was called with the same index shortly before, indicating a float click.
  API version: 1

linkToLastTweaked(int controlIndex, int channel, (int globalLink, int eventID)) -> int
  Arguments: int controlIndex, int channel, (int globalLink, int eventID)
  Returns: int
  Description: this function will create a regular (or global) controller link for the last tweaked parameter. set optional eventID to assign link to specific control instead of last tweaked control function returns (0) on success, (1) when nothing was tweaked or (2) when control is in use
  API version: 21

midiOutMsg(int message) -> None [overload 1]
  Arguments: int message
  Returns: -
  Description: Send a MIDI message to the (linked) output interface - "message" holds the value to be sent, with the channel and command in the lower byte and the first and second data values in the next two bytes.
  API version: 1

midiOutMsg(int midiId, int channel, int data1, int data2) -> None [overload 2]
  Arguments: int midiId, int channel, int data1, int data2
  Returns: -
  Description: Send a MIDI message to the (linked) output interface (alternative version with separate parameters)
  API version: 2

midiOutNewMsg(int slotIndex, int message) -> None
  Arguments: int slotIndex, int message
  Returns: -
  Description: Send a MIDI message to the (linked) output interface, but only if the value has changed - "slotIndex" is a value chosen by the caller, it should be the same as it was for the previous message that should be compared with - "message" holds the value to be sent.
  API version: 1

midiOutSysex(string message) -> None
  Arguments: string message
  Returns: -
  Description: Send a SYSEX message to the (linked) output interface.
  API version: 1

processMIDICC(eventData) -> None
  Arguments: eventData
  Returns: -
  Description: Let FL process a CC message - use this function inside OnMidiMsg and pass (modified) eventData object as function parameter
  API version: 1

